Verse 1:
[D]The [G]day Thou [D]gavest, [Em]Lor[Am]d, is [D7]ended, [C]The [D7]dar[G]k[D7]ness [Em]falls at [A]Thy [A7]be[D]hest;
[D]To [G]Thee our [D]morning [Em]hym[Am]ns as[D7]cended, [C]Thy [G]praise [D7]shall [Em]hal[G][Am]low now [D7]our [G]rest.

Verse 2:
[D][G]We [D][Em]thank [Am][D7]Thee [C][D7]that [G][D7]Thy [Em][A]church, [A7][D]unsleeping
[D][G][D]while [Em][Am]earth [D7][C]rolls [G][D7][Em]onward [G][Am]into [D7][G]light,
[D][G]through [D][Em]all [Am][D7]the [C]world [D7][G]her [D7][Em]watch [A][A7]is [D]keeping,
[D][G]and [D][Em]rests [Am][D7]not [C]now [G][D7]by [Em][G]day [Am][D7]or [G]night.

Verse 3:
[D][G][D]As [Em][Am]o'er [D7][C]each [D7][G][D7]continent [Em][A]and [A7][D]island
